.TH "waybar\-niri\-workspaces" "5" "2026\-08\-07"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- niri workspaces module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBworkspaces\fR module displays the currently used workspaces in niri.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Addressed by \fBniri/workspaces\fR
.PP
\fBall\-outputs\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to false, workspaces will only be shown on the output they are on.\& If set to true all workspaces will be shown on every output.\&
.PP
\fBsort\-by\-name\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Sort workspaces by name (numeric sort when all names are numbers).\& Unnamed workspaces fall back to their index on the output.\&
.PP
\fBsort\-by\-coordinates\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Sort workspaces by output and index.\& If both \fBsort\-by\-name\fR and \fBsort\-by\-coordinates\fR are true, sorting by name is applied.\&
.PP
\fBsort\-by\-id\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Sort workspaces by id, taking precedence over other sort options.\&
.PP
\fBsort\-by\-number\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Deprecated alias for \fBsort\-by\-id\fR; prefer \fBsort\-by\-id\fR instead.\&
.PP
If none of the sorting options are enabled, workspaces keep their output/index order.\&
.PP
\fBformat\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: {value} 
.br
The format, how information should be displayed.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-icons\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
Based on the workspace name, index and state, the corresponding icon gets selected.\& See \fBicons\fR.\&
.PP
\fBdisable\-click\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to false, you can click to change workspace.\& If set to true this behaviour is disabled.\&
.PP
\fBenable\-bar\-scroll\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to false, you can'\&t scroll to cycle throughout workspaces from the entire bar.\& If set to true this behaviour is enabled.\&
.PP
\fBdisable\-markup\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, button label will escape pango markup.\&
.PP
\fBcurrent\-only\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, only the active or focused workspace will be shown.\&
.PP
\fBdisplay\-condition\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
oneof: "show\-all", "keep\-named", "only\-populated" 
.br
default: "show\-all" 
.br
Specifies the conditions for showing workspace widgets.\& 
.br

.br
\fBshow\-all\fR: displays widgets for all workspaces.\& 
.br
\fBkeep\-named\fR: always displays named workspaces, irrespective of whether they contain windows or not.\& 
.br
\fBonly\-populated\fR: only displays widgets for workspaces that have windows.\&
.PP
\fBhide\-empty\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, empty workspaces will not be shown.\&
.PP
\fBon\-update\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Command to execute when the module is updated.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables this module to consume all left over space dynamically.\&
.RS 4
.PP
.RE
\fBworkspace\-taskbar\fR: 
.br
typeof: object 
.br
Contains settings for the workspace taskbar, which displays app icons within each workspace.\&
.PP
.RS 4
\fBenable\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables the workspace taskbar mode.\&
.PP
\fBicon\-size\fR: 
.br
typeof: int 
.br
default: 16 
.br
Size of the icons in the workspace taskbar.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBignore\-workspaces\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
default: [] 
.br
Regexes to match against workspaces names and index'\&s.\& If there'\&s a match, the workspace will not be shown.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-window\-separator\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: " " 
.br
Separator used between window representations generated by \fBwindow\-rewrite\fR.\&
.PP
\fBwindow\-rewrite\fR: 
.br
typeof: object 
.br
default: {} 
.br
Rules to map window app_id and/or title to a specific string representation (e.\&g.\&, an icon).\& Keys are regular expressions matching `app_id<regex>` and/or `title<regex>`.\& Values are the replacement strings, which can contain `{app_id}` and `{title}` placeholders.\&
.PP
\fBwindow\-rewrite\-default\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: "?\&" 
.br
The default representation for windows that don'\&t match any rule in \fBwindow\-rewrite\fR.\&
.PP
.SH FORMAT REPLACEMENTS
.PP
\fB{value}\fR: Name of the workspace, or index for unnamed workspaces,
as defined by niri.\&
.PP
\fB{name}\fR: Name of the workspace for named workspaces.\&
.PP
\fB{icon}\fR: Icon, as defined in \fBformat\-icons\fR.\&
.PP
\fB{index}\fR: Index of the workspace on its output.\&
.PP
\fB{output}\fR: Output where the workspace is located.\&
.PP
\fB{total}\fR: The total number of workspaces.\&
.PP
\fB{windows}\fR: Concatenated representation of windows in the workspace, using \fBwindow\-rewrite\fR rules and \fBformat\-window\-separator\fR.\&
.PP
.SH ICONS
.PP
Additional to workspace name matching, the following \fBformat\-icons\fR can be set.\&
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBdefault\fR: Will be shown, when no string matches are found.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBfocused\fR: Will be shown, when workspace is focused.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBactive\fR: Will be shown, when workspace is active on its output.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBurgent\fR: Will be shown, when workspace has urgent windows.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBempty\fR: Will be shown, when workspace is empty.\&
.PD
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"niri/workspaces": {
    "format": "{icon} {windows}",
    "format\-window\-separator": "|",
    "window\-rewrite\-default": "",
    "window\-rewrite": {
        "app_id<firefox>": "",
        "app_id<foot>": "",
        "app_id<org\&.gnome\&.Nautilus> title<\&.*Downloads\&.*>": "",
        "app_id<org\&.gnome\&.Nautilus>": ""
    },
    "format\-icons": {
        // Named workspaces
        // (you need to configure them in niri)
        "browser": "",
        "discord": "",
        "chat": "<b></b>",

        // Icons by state
        "active": "",
        "default": ""
    }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"niri/workspaces": {
    "format": "{icon}",
    "workspace\-taskbar": {
        "enable": true,
        "icon\-size": 18
    }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
